Provenance of reused visual assets:

  The emblem vector (FAIRY_EMBLEM in lib/client.js) is taken from the original
  plugin published by the Bilibili author 天才小宇
  (https://space.bilibili.com/3494360513514129 ; video BV1n7np6QEPe), distributed
  there as the local package @local/dsh-hdd-overlay. It is not a redraw.

  Part of the visual stylesheet is taken from the same plugin as well: the grid
  texture, the vignette, the panel veil, and the --hdd-* custom-property names.

  The rest of this package is written for this repository: the launch timeline,
  the nine /hdd/* media routes, the asset settings page, the cue state machine,
  the skin-manager wiring, the tests and the documentation.

  The design and flow themselves are credited, not claimed: the splash sequence
  (HDD boot -> emblem -> greeting -> flight back to the sidebar) follows the
  reference video linked above.

Design reference:

  The visual language of the splash timeline (emblem rise, hold, flight to the
  sidebar) follows the same reference. Fairy-DSH
  (https://github.com/Chengzhibense/Fairy-DSH, Apache-2.0) is credited as an
  earlier project in that lineage.

